<p>The foundation of your documentation begins with the vehicle’s identity and legal status. You must provide a **self-attested photocopy of the Registration Certificate (RC)**. This document verifies ownership and must be clearly visible and legible. Alongside the RC, you need to submit proof of a **current Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate**.</p>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">A valid PUC ensures that your vehicle meets environmental standards and is roadworthy, which is a mandatory check for any vehicle entering or exiting specific zones.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Furthermore, a **valid insurance certificate** is non-negotiable.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>This certificate must be in force for the entire duration of the transit period, covering any potential incidents that may occur while the vehicle is in the transporter’s custody.</span></li></ul>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Beyond standard vehicle documents, the logistics of the transport service itself require specific commercial paperwork.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>You must ensure that an **IBA-approved consignment bilty** is generated for the shipment.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The International Biryani Association (IBA) standard, often adapted in local logistics contexts for standardized billing and tracking, ensures that the consignment is properly documented for interstate or intrastate movement.</span></li></ul>
<p>This bilty acts as a contract between you and the transporter, detailing the route, estimated delivery time, and terms of liability. Without this approved document, the transporter may refuse to accept the vehicle, or you may face issues during checkpoint inspections.</p>

<p>To fully protect your investment, it is crucial to highlight the importance of **100% declared-value marine transit insurance**. Standard third-party insurance often falls short in covering the full value of your vehicle in the event of total loss or major damage during transit.</p>
<p>By opting for 100% declared-value coverage, you ensure that you are compensated for the exact market value of your car, as agreed upon at the time of booking. This comprehensive coverage minimizes financial risk and provides a safety net against unforeseen accidents, theft, or natural disasters en route.</p>

